diff --git a/docs/api-specification.md b/docs/api-specification.md
index ba9f337..cdb42d6 100644
--- a/docs/api-specification.md
+++ b/docs/api-specification.md
@@ -48,3 +48,20 @@ Public and safe to repeat. Ends the session and clears the cookie. Returns 204.
 
 Requires a session. Returns 200 `{ "data": { "user": {...} } }`, or
 401 `UNAUTHENTICATED`.
+
+## POST /onboarding
+
+Requires a session. Completes account setup in one transaction.
+
+Body: `capabilities` (1-2 of professional, client), `displayName` (1-80),
+`headline` (optional, max 120), `location` (optional, max 80),
+`skills` (0-15 names, max 40 characters each), `interests` (0-8 codes),
+`goals` (1+ codes).
+
+- 201: `{ "data": { "user": {..., "capabilities", "onboardedAt" } } }`
+- 400 `VALIDATION_ERROR` (with `details`, for example field `skills.2`)
+- 401 `UNAUTHENTICATED`
+- 409 `ONBOARDING_ALREADY_COMPLETED`
+
+`GET /auth/me` and the login/register responses now include `capabilities`
+and `onboardedAt`.
diff --git a/docs/database-schema.md b/docs/database-schema.md
index 460b0d2..a55da59 100644
--- a/docs/database-schema.md
+++ b/docs/database-schema.md
@@ -29,3 +29,24 @@ Notes:
 | expires_at | timestamp | 7 days after login                                                     |
 
 Expired rows are ignored when reading. A cleanup job comes later.
+
+## users (new columns)
+
+- `capabilities` account_type[]: what the account can do (`professional`, `client`).
+  Strict database enum, because it affects permissions.
+- `onboarded_at` timestamp, null until onboarding is finished.
+
+## profiles
+
+One per user (`user_id` unique, cascade delete): `display_name`, `headline`,
+`location`, `interests` text[], `goals` text[], timestamps.
+Part 4 adds bio, experience, education, portfolio, and visibility.
+
+## skills
+
+Shared catalog: `name` (display text) and `name_key` (lowercase, unique).
+
+## user_skills
+
+Join table. Composite primary key (`user_id`, `skill_id`): the same skill
+cannot be added twice. Index on `skill_id`. Cascade delete.
